this strain of coronavirus is related to  the common cold as well as the more  serious and highly infectious SARS or  severe acute respiratory syndrome at the  moment there is no vaccine or known cure  for this new virus what we do know is  that it most likely passed from animals  to humans in a market in the Chinese  city of Wuhan and it's believed to have  likely originated in bats Chinese  scientists were able to quickly identify  its genetic sequence allowing  researchers across the world to start  work on treatments in Australia  officials say they've developed  lab-grown version of the virus which  would be a major step towards creating a  vaccine drugs used to fight HIV and  influenza have been tested in China as  possible treatments and officials say  they are showing promising science  however the World Health Organization  has played down reports of any kind of  breakthrough but some drug makers are  expected to begin vaccine tests on  humans possibly within 3 months that may  seem a while away but this process has  traditionally taken years right now some  of the best ways to prevent the spread  of corona virus is to avoid contact with  those showing symptoms washing your  hands regularly and covering your mouth  when coughing or sneezing
 

